Building the YaKlock binary package
===================================

Install build-essential and debhelper from your distribution, then run this
command from the source checkout:

    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The output is ../yaklock_0.7-1_all.deb. The package is architecture-independent
and can be built and used on amd64 without bundling any libraries. Update the
version in debian/changelog for subsequent releases.

Install a local copy with:

    sudo apt install ./yaklock_0.7-1_all.deb

APT uses the system Python 3, PyGObject, Pycairo, and GTK 3. The package places
the executable, desktop entry, and hicolor icons under /usr. If an earlier
manual installation exists in ~/.local, it can take precedence in the desktop
menu or PATH. Use /usr/bin/yaklock to launch the packaged copy directly.

YaKlock still uses ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/yaklock/options.json
and its adjacent lock file. Installation, upgrade, removal, and purge do
not change those per-user files.

The dependency floors target Debian 12 and Ubuntu 22.04 or newer. Always on
Top uses X11 or XWayland when available and depends on the window manager.

Build automation
================

The Debian package workflow runs on relevant pull requests and supports
manual runs. It builds on an amd64 Ubuntu runner, verifies the packaged
executable, desktop entry, and icons, and uploads the .deb and SHA256SUMS
as a GitHub Actions artifact. Each build has its own checksum.

Validation of the accepted package
==================================

Package: yaklock_0.7-1_all.deb
SHA256: 47b41ef229ab3381227c9bcf60ca2765bcb7bc0296d5b0a1c84e2beb651d0f42

* Interactive GNOME on lappy: PASS, owner UAT accepted.
* Upgrade from an older installed package on lappy: INCONCLUSIVE.
* A transient dpkg-preconfigure warning appeared during owner UAT and did
  not recur in subsequent testing.
* Separate packaging checks on Ubuntu 26.04 amd64: APT install simulation,
  isolated dpkg install, prepared version-to-version upgrade, removal and
  purge, with existing preferences and lock file preserved. Concurrent
  saves to different preferences survived reload.
* The packaged launcher opened a window and the bundled icon resolved
  in live KDE Plasma and headless GNOME Shell/Mutter, both over XWayland.
